a92476ba3a4", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Elementary Social Studies Inquiry Capstone", "description": "Students synthesize the course by designing, justifying, and revising a standards-aligned inquiry unit for elementary learners.", "children": [{"id": "1fd2d657-132a-483c-bbab-f482c02a1a80", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inquiry unit proposal", "children": [{"id": "873032ac-15b7-4a50-89dc-a6621228ebea", "type": "concept", "title": "Compelling question, supporting questions, and rationale"}, {"id": "da025f46-219b-4592-9dbe-06c9652ce441", "type": "concept", "title": "NCSS/C3/state standards and grade-level fit"}, {"id": "f1619d8c-2250-4d88-8e9b-4c12d339fc93", "type": "concept", "title": "History, geography, civics, economics, culture, and local/community connections"}], "description": "Students design a unit around a compelling question, standards, disciplinary thinking, and civic purpose."}, {"id": "72231552-1843-4b77-8721-e23ec2ce8d63", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Teaching artifact", "children": [{"id": "ae39e95d-4f0a-4b4f-a9e3-e061567652d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Lesson sequence, source set, map task, discussion protocol, and civic action option"}, {"id": "af676042-e8a9-4804-a5fa-debdffb3226e", "type": "concept", "title": "Differentiation, UDL, multilingual supports, and family/community links"}, {"id": "982fdb15-a69c-4667-b15b-1e7e874ed908", "type": "concept", "title": "Rubric, formative checks, and summative performance task"}], "description": "Students produce a teachable sequence with materials, supports, and assessment."}, {"id": "b02f355f-47fa-43bf-a2d4-689de49121cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflection and revision", "children": [{"id": "a3b879e2-4582-4207-8a53-72c5c75c1a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-based rationale and implementation plan"}, {"id": "b4bd5566-51bd-4536-9853-0d6a3d338114", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer, instructor, and learner feedback cycles"}, {"id": "a18ca286-dad6-4176-865a-c8804f724ad9", "type": "c